PHP 5.3.29 backport of php/php-src 712e60f9edfd03f0960fc4fc3c2c375f42b90aa2
https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/712e60f9edfd03f0960fc4fc3c2c375f42b90aa2
CVE-2026-109618 / GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w: allocation failures exit without bailout.
CVE-2026-109619 / GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp: clear request-owned state at shutdown.

Adapted to Zend Engine 2, TSRMLS and GNU89. PHP 5.3 has no session upload
progress. Its concat opcodes use zend_operators.c; its safe_address helper
lives in zend_alloc.c. PHP 7 singleton-array/SIMD optimizations are not
ported to the different PHP 5 hash representation. Multipart header filtering
and a body-part limit reduce memory amplification independently.

This follows the upstream minimal EOL mitigation, not the full supported-
branch redesign. Hard allocation failures intentionally skip PHP shutdown
functions, destructors and output flushing, terminating the worker with 1.

